---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Input trust — .NET Challenges"
  description="Practice keeping a server-owned price when a JSON create or replace sends its own."
>
  <main id="main" class="challenge">
    <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href={base}>All available challenges</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">Input trust</span>
    </nav>

    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="challenge-title">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Sequence 02 <span>/ 09</span> · API ACTION</p>
        <h1 id="challenge-title">Input trust</h1>
        <p class="hero-summary">
          Store the title the client sent, and keep the price the server owns.
        </p>
      </div>
      <aside class="status-slip" aria-label="Example create and its required effect">
        <div class="slip-top">
          <span>Request trace</span>
          <span>01 / 04</span>
        </div>
        <code class="slip-route">POST /listings</code>
        <pre><code>{`{ "title": "Lamp", "price": 1 }`}</code></pre>
        <p class="slip-result">
          <span class="stamp">201</span>
          <span>title Lamp, price 20</span>
        </p>
        <p class="slip-result">
          <span class="state-mark" aria-hidden="true">=</span>
          <span>stored price stays 20</span>
        </p>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <div class="content-grid">
      <div class="main-column">
        <section class="content-section decision" aria-labelledby="decision-title">
          <p class="section-kicker">The decision</p>
          <h2 id="decision-title">
            A create or replace stores the title from the JSON body and keeps the stored
            price at 20. A price in that body does not change the stored price, and the
            title is still stored.
          </h2>
        </section>

        <section class="content-section effects" aria-labelledby="effects-title">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <div>
              <p class="section-kicker">What a local pass proves</p>
              <h2 id="effects-title">Required effects</h2>
            </div>
            <span class="effect-count">4 checks</span>
          </div>
          <p class="effect-contract">
            Each test starts from an empty listing store. No test observes another test's
            listings. The result does not depend on order. The harness sends
            <code>Content-Type: application/json</code> and does not send a form body. It
            matches <code>id</code>, <code>title</code>, and <code>price</code> without
            regard to case. The title value is the exact string that was sent. The price
            value is the number 20. The id may be a number or a string; the read and the
            replace use the id from the create body. Extra JSON members on a response do
            not fail a check. The harness does not send a client id or the price 20.
          </p>
          <ol class="effect-list">
            <li>
              <span class="effect-number">01</span>
              <p>
                <code>POST /listings</code> with <code>{`{ "title": "Lamp", "price": 1 }`}</code>
                returns 201 and JSON whose title is <code>Lamp</code> and whose price is 20,
                with an id. <code>GET /listings/{`{id}`}</code> returns 200 and the same title,
                price, and id.
              </p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="effect-number">02</span>
              <p>
                <code>POST /listings</code> with <code>{`{ "title": "Lamp" }`}</code> returns
                201 with title <code>Lamp</code> and price 20. The following GET returns that
                title and price.
              </p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="effect-number">03</span>
              <p>
                <code>POST /listings</code> with <code>{`{ "title": "Lamp" }`}</code> returns
                201 with price 20. <code>PUT /listings/{`{id}`}</code> with
                <code>{`{ "title": "Shade", "price": 1 }`}</code> returns 204. The following
                GET returns title <code>Shade</code> and price 20.
              </p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="effect-number">04</span>
              <p>
                <code>POST /listings</code> with <code>{`{ "title": "Lamp", "price": 1 }`}</code>
                returns 201 with price 20. <code>PUT /listings/{`{id}`}</code> with
                <code>{`{ "title": "Shade" }`}</code> returns 204. The following GET returns
                title <code>Shade</code> and price 20.
              </p>
            </li>
          </ol>
          <p class="effect-boundary">
            A replace of an id that is not stored is outside the effects. Title validation,
            including an empty title, is outside the effects. A client-supplied id, a problem
            response, and a form body are outside the effects.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="content-section guidance" aria-labelledby="hints-title">
          <p class="section-kicker">Ask for a nudge</p>
          <h2 id="hints-title">Hints</h2>
          <div class="disclosures">
            <details data-reveal="input-trust-hint-1" data-hint-number="1">
              <summary><span>Hint 1</span><span class="summary-label">Name the behavior</span></summary>
              <p>
                A create or replace stores the title from the body and keeps the stored price
                at 20, including when the body includes a price. Rejecting that body because
                it includes a price still fails, because the title is not stored.
              </p>
            </details>
            <div data-hint-gate="2" hidden>
              <details data-reveal="input-trust-hint-2" data-hint-number="2">
                <summary><span>Hint 2</span><span class="summary-label">Find the framework area</span></summary>
                <p>Input models.</p>
              </details>
            </div>
            <div data-hint-gate="3" hidden>
              <details data-reveal="input-trust-hint-3" data-hint-number="3">
                <summary><span>Hint 3</span><span class="summary-label">Narrow the approach</span></summary>
                <p>
                  Take only the title from the JSON body, set the stored price to 20 on
                  create, and leave the stored price unchanged on replace. Limiting the bound
                  form fields still fails, because this body is JSON and the sent price is
                  stored.
                </p>
              </details>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="content-section solution" aria-labelledby="solution-title">
          <p class="section-kicker">See one working approach</p>
          <h2 id="solution-title">Reference solution</h2>
          <details data-reveal="input-trust-reference">
            <summary><span>Open the reference solution</span><span class="summary-label">Optional</span></summary>
            <div class="solution-copy">
              <p>
                The reference solution uses a write body that has a title and no price.
                Create copies that title onto a stored listing and sets the price to 20.
                Replace copies that title onto the listing already stored for that id and
                does not change its price. The handlers do not read a price from the body.
                A price in the JSON is outside the write body, so it is not stored, and the
                title still is. Create returns 201 with the stored id, title, and price.
                Replace returns 204. The read returns the stored listing. The other valid
                approach is to bind a listing that still has a price and, in both handlers,
                copy only the title, set 20 on create, and keep the stored price on replace.
                The trade-off is that the bound listing still carries the client's price, so
                saving that listing stores the client price again. The plausible miss is a
                binding attribute that limits which form fields bind. That attribute does not
                apply to a JSON body, so a sent price is still stored.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </section>
      </div>

      <aside class="side-column" aria-label="Challenge setup">
        <section class="run-card" aria-labelledby="run-title">
          <p class="section-kicker">Your local proof</p>
          <h2 id="run-title">Clone, then test</h2>
          <p>
            Challenge directory: <code>input-trust</code>
          </p>
          <p>Setup: git and the .NET SDK.</p>
          <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/mustafaAshfaq/dotnet-challenges.git
cd dotnet-challenges/input-trust
dotnet test</code></pre>
          <a
            class="repo-link"
            href="https://github.com/mustafaAshfaq/dotnet-challenges/tree/main/input-trust"
          >
            Browse the challenge directory
          </a>
        </section>
        <section class="prerequisite" aria-labelledby="prerequisite-title">
          <p class="section-kicker" id="prerequisite-title">Prerequisite</p>
          <p>
            <a href={`${base}challenges/request-validation/`}>HTTP API contracts</a>.
            Advisory only: this challenge stays readable, cloneable, and completable
            without it.
          </p>
        </section>
        <p class="completion-note">
          This catalog shows the requirements. The code and the proof run on your machine.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .challenge {
    padding-block: 1.5rem 2rem;
  }

  .crumbs {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.65rem;
    min-height: 2.75rem;
    margin-block-end: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
  }

  .crumbs a {
    min-height: 2.75rem;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  .hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.1fr) minmax(17rem, 22rem);
    align-items: end;
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3.5rem);
    padding-block: clamp(1rem, 3vw, 2rem) 0.5rem;
  }

  .hero .eyebrow {
    margin-block-end: 1rem;
  }

  .hero .eyebrow span {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  h1,
  h2,
  h3,
  p {
    margin-block-start: 0;
  }

  h1 {
    max-width: 12ch;
    margin-block-end: 0.9rem;
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    line-height: 0.98;
  }

  .hero-summary {
    max-width: 36ch;
    margin-block-end: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.8vw, 1.25rem);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .content-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(18rem, 22rem);
    align-items: start;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4.5rem);
    padding-block-start: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
  }

  .hero,
  .content-grid,
  .main-column,
  .side-column,
  .run-card {
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .content-section + .content-section {
    margin-block-start: clamp(2.8rem, 5vw, 4rem);
  }

  .section-kicker {
    margin-block-end: 0.7rem;
  }

  .content-section h2 {
    margin-block-end: 0;
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.2rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    line-height: 1.15;
  }

  .decision h2 {
    max-width: 62ch;
    padding-inline-start: 1rem;
    border-inline-start: 3px solid var(--fail);
    font-family: var(--body);
    font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 2vw, 1.4rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .section-heading {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-end;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-block-end: 1.2rem;
  }

  .effect-count {
    padding: 0.25rem 0.55rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--muted);
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .effect-contract,
  .effect-boundary {
    max-width: 68ch;
    margin-block: 1rem 0;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .effect-list {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    list-style: none;
    border-block-start: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .effect-list li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2.5rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0.9rem;
    padding-block: 1.2rem;
    border-block-end: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .effect-number {
    width: 2rem;
    height: 2rem;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--pass);
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .effect-list p {
    max-width: 68ch;
    margin-block-end: 0;
  }

  code,
  pre {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }

  p code,
  h2 code,
  li code {
    padding: 0.08rem 0.28rem;
    background: var(--mark);
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .side-column {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .run-card {
    padding: 1.2rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-top: 4px solid var(--pass);
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .run-card h2 {
    margin-block-end: 0.55rem;
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }

  .run-card > p:not(.section-kicker) {
    margin-block-end: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }

  .run-card pre {
    max-width: 100%;
    overflow-x: auto;
    padding: 0.85rem;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    background: var(--ink);
    color: #f4f7f5;
    line-height: 1.7;
    white-space: pre;
  }

  .repo-link {
    min-height: 2.75rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .prerequisite {
    padding: 1rem 1.2rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: var(--mark);
  }

  .prerequisite .section-kicker {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .prerequisite p:last-child {
    margin-block-end: 0;
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  .completion-note {
    margin-block: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
  }

  .disclosures {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.65rem;
    margin-block-start: 1.15rem;
  }

  details {
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  summary {
    min-height: 3.25rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 0.65rem 0.9rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    cursor: pointer;
    font-weight: 700;
    list-style: none;
    transition: background-color 180ms ease-out;
  }

  summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  summary::after {
    width: 1.75rem;
    height: 1.75rem;
    flex: none;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 50%;
    color: var(--pass);
    content: "+";
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  details[open] > summary::after {
    content: "−";
  }

  summary:hover {
    background: var(--canvas);
  }

  summary:active {
    background: var(--mark);
  }

  .summary-label {
    margin-inline-start: auto;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    text-align: right;
  }

  details > p,
  .solution-copy {
    padding: 0 0.95rem 1rem;
    margin-block-end: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .solution-copy p:last-child {
    margin-block-end: 0;
  }

  .solution > h2 {
    margin-block-end: 1rem;
  }

  .solution details {
    border-color: var(--line);
    background: var(--mark);
  }

  .solution details > summary {
    min-height: 3.5rem;
  }

  .solution-copy {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  [hidden] {
    display: none !important;
  }

  @media (min-width: 961px) {
    .side-column {
      position: sticky;
      top: 1.25rem;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    .hero,
    .content-grid,
    .side-column {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .status-slip {
      order: -1;
      max-width: 28rem;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .challenge {
      padding-block-start: 0.75rem;
    }

    .crumbs {
      font-size: 0.8rem;
    }

    .status-slip {
      max-width: none;
    }

    .effect-list li {
      grid-template-columns: 2rem minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 0.65rem;
    }

    .effect-number {
      width: 1.75rem;
      height: 1.75rem;
    }

    .summary-label {
      font-size: 0.72rem;
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    summary {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
</style>
